From: CardSat <https://github.com/prstoetzer/CardSat>
Subject: [PATCH] add clearLastError() so lastError() means "this operation"

lastError_ is cleared only in begin(), so any timeout anywhere in a session is still
reported afterwards. A caller testing lastError() after end() to decide whether the
teardown succeeded gets false positives from unrelated earlier failures -- a bulk OUT
the device never drained, a control transfer it ignored. We spent considerable time
chasing a teardown bug that did not exist because of this.

--- a/src/EspUsbHost.h
+++ b/src/EspUsbHost.h
@@
   int lastError() const;
+  // Clear the sticky error so a following operation's lastError() reflects only that
+  // operation. lastError_ is otherwise cleared only in begin().
+  void clearLastError();

--- a/src/EspUsbHost.cpp
+++ b/src/EspUsbHost.cpp
@@ after EspUsbHost::ready()
+void EspUsbHost::clearLastError()
+{
+  lastError_ = ESP_OK;
+}
